    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "SITE FOR SALE\r\nCIRCA 0.096 ACRES\r\nMAIN STREET, KILFENORA, CO. CLARE.\r\n\r\nFOR SALE SUBJECT TO PLANNING PERMISSION\r\nCONTAINED IN FOLIO CE12903\r\nVIEWINGS STRICTLY BY ADVANCE APPOINTMENT WITH SOLE AGENT STREETS AHEAD PROPERTIES\r\n\r\nPROPERTY LICENCE NO 003178\r\n\r\nDESCRIPTION:\r\n\r\nStreets Ahead Properties are delighted to bring to the market this site circa 0.0391 hectares (0.096 acres) contained in Folio CE12903 with circa 18.8 meters of road frontage.\r\n\r\nA rare opportunity to acquire a well-located site of approximately 0.391 hectares 0.096 acres on Main Street, Kilfenora, Co. Clare on the R481. Situated in the heart of this charming and historic village, the site offers excellent potential for a variety of uses, subject to the necessary planning permission. With its central location and convenient access to local amenities, services and surrounding attractions, this property represents an attractive opportunity for those looking to develop in one of County Clare’s most sought-after village locations.\r\n\r\nKilfenora is a small and historic village in County Clare, Ireland, located on the edge of the Burren, a unique limestone landscape famous for its rocky scenery and rich variety of plants. The village is best known for Kilfenora Cathedral, which dates back to the 12th century, and its impressive High Crosses. Kilfenora has a strong connection to traditional Irish music and is often associated with the famous Kilfenora Céilí Band. With its beautiful surroundings, fascinating history and traditional character, Kilfenora is an important and interesting place to visit in County Clare."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "All facilities close by\r\nConvenient to local schools, shops, cafés, pubs, and everyday amenities.\r\nGood road access to Ennistymon, Lahinch, Ennis, and Shannon Airport.\r\nExcellent base for enjoying the Burren and surrounding countryside\r\nDevelopment potential\r\n0.096 acres\r\nSuitable opportunity for those looking to build a home in a scenic rural village setting"
      }
    ],
